# XSH getresuid
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
# getresuid() stores the real, effective and saved IDs. The saved ID has no
# other defined relation to the process, so only the real and effective IDs
# are compared with getuid() and geteuid(), and the three values are compared
# across fork() and after a child changed them.

assertion  XSH.getresuid.001
anchor     functions/getresuid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getresuid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2024
says       getresuid() returns 0 and the real and effective user IDs it stores equal
           getuid() and geteuid(); a forked child sees the same three values.
test       t/001-matches.c

assertion  XSH.getresuid.002
anchor     functions/getresuid.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2024
says       After a child changes its user IDs with setresuid() to three different
           values, getresuid() in the child reports exactly those three.
needs      root
test       t/002-after-change.c
